  dialogueLines:
  - subtitleText: "After the liberation, the British military tribunal sought justice.
      In the autumn of 1945, the Belsen Trials were held in the nearby town of L\xFCneburg.
      Forty-five SS members and kapos, including Commandant Kramer, stood trial for
      their horrific war crimes and crimes against humanity."
